uneven:
To draw my uses to cohere with needs,
And bring the uneven world back to its round;
Or, failing so much, fill up, bridge at least

une:
scented hair,
Une jolie fille à vendre, très cher;
A thing of gaiety, a thing of sorrow,

unerring:
She feels the iron hand of pain no more;
The dispensations of unerring grace,
Should turn your sorrows into grateful praise;

unexpressed:
My heart was filled with unvoiced cries
And prayers and pleadings unexpressed;
But while I burned with Love's unrest,

unequall'd:
Thy wonted auditories cease to throng.
Thy sermons in unequall'd accents flow'd,
And ev'ry bosom with devotion glow'd;

unembittered:
And I tried to take their stings
With gay unembittered lips;
That I loved with all my strength,
